# Frontend is served by Go

Do not treat `npm run dev` / Vite `:5173` as the way to show frontend changes to the user.

After changing anything under `web/src` (or other files that affect the UI):

1. Rebuild: `npm run build` in `web/` (writes `web/dist`).
2. Run the Go server with `-web web/dist`, for example:

```text
go run ./cmd/server -addr 127.0.0.1:8080 -web web/dist ...
```

Match the data-source flags the user is already using (do not switch synthetic/tushare just to preview UI). If `:8080` is occupied by an older `cmd/server`, stop it and restart so it picks up the new `web/dist`.

Verify in the browser at the Go address (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:8080`), not Vite.
